WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:06.370
The Sopranos was the first jewel in HBO's
"Prestige TV" crown, known for its unpredictable

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:11.780
plot, gritty realism, and introducing the
word 'gabagool' to people outside of New Jersey

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.520
"Gabagool?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:13.900
Over here!"

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.500
But perhaps the biggest key to the show's
success was the talented ensemble cast, most

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.640
of whom we learned to love and hate in equal
measure over the course of six unforgettable

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.140
seasons.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.980
Here's where your favorite Sopranos actors
are now.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.440
Edie Falco as Carmela Soprano

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.900
Critical acclaim followed Edie Falco into
her first major post-Sopranos project, Showtime's

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:40.210
Nurse Jackie, with the Brooklyn-born actress
playing the namesake role in the edgy dramedy,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.719
from 2009 until it came to an end in 2015.

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:49.409
She later moved on to Louis C.K.'s popular
2016 web series Horace and Pete and has dabbled

00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:54.629
in movies in recent years, though she hasn't
left TV behind; her recent projects include

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:58.280
the Law and Order miniseries True Crime: The
Menendez Murders.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.260
Robert Iler as A.J.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:00.760
Soprano

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.660
After The Sopranos, Robert Iler gave up acting
for poker, moving to Las Vegas in 2012 so

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:11.700
he could focus on the World Series of Poker
full-time after entering the high-stakes competition

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.740
on a handful of occasions as a youngster.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.030
He says his obsession with card games started
when his grandmother taught him how to play

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.080
Rummy and Gin.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.500
Jamie-Lynn Sigler as Meadow Soprano

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:26.580
Like Robert Iler, Jamie-Lynn Sigler peaked
early with the The Sopranos, never managing

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.900
to outgrow it despite her best efforts.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.450
She tried to launch a career in pop music
during the show's run, though when that died

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.760
and her time as Meadow ended, opportunities
were hard to come by.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.700
The real reason for her sparse filmography
was revealed in 2016, when the actress admitted

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.600
that she had been suffering from MS for almost
15 years, saying the last time she had the

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.800
energy to run was while filming the Sopranos
finale.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.880
Michael Imperioli as Christopher Moltisanti

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.680
In the years since his character was killed
off by Tony, Michael Imperioli hasn't managed

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.940
to find the same levels of acclaim he enjoyed
while playing the tragic Christopher, as a

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:05.470
quick glance at his splat-heavy Rotten Tomatoes
record proves.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:10.640
Of his last 15 films reviewed by the website's
network of critics, 13 have been declared

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.140
rotten.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:16.920
In the Spring of 2017, he was lured back to
television, appearing as Zach Braff's right-hand

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.290
hand man in the ABC comedy Alex, Inc..

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.060
Drea de Matteo as Adriana La Cerva

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:27.510
While Queens-born actress Drea de Matteo has
dabbled in film from time to time, she's stuck

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:32.360
with TV for the most part since meeting her
end in The Sopranos: she played Joey Tribbiani's

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:37.560
sister Gina in his short-lived Friends spinoff,
brassy Italian-American Angie in Desperate

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:42.800
Housewives, and Jax's ex-wife Wendy in Sons
of Anarchy before supporting Jennifer Lopez

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.340
in the NBC cop drama Shades of Blue.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.820
Steven Van Zandt as Silvio Dante

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.760
A guitarist in Bruce Springsteen's E Street
Band, Steven Van Zandt had never acted in

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.750
a major role before portraying Silvio Dante
on The Sopranos.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:01.200
After his character was left comatose in the
finale, he went back to music, of course,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.760
but also had a stint on Lilyhammer, the first-ever
Netflix original series.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.110
Netflix pulled the plug in 2015, canceling
the show after three seasons, and Van Zandt

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.280
hasn't on-screen in anything since.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.720
Tony Sirico as Paulie Walnuts

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:21.430
Real-life ex-con and self-described former
"pistol-packin' guy" Tony Sirico reunited

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:26.940
with Steven Van Zandt in Lilyhammer for two
episodes starting in 2013, and with Woody

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:32.270
Allen for 2016's Cafe Society, having appeared
in the past in Allen's Bullets Over Broadway

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.920
and Deconstructing Harry.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.760
Sirico hasn't done much in the years since,
though he occasionally cashes in on his tough

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.140
guy image with cameos.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.540
Dominic Chianese as Uncle Junior

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.980
Best known for his role as Tony's pain-in-the-ass
Uncle Junior, Dominic Chianese plied his trade

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:53.300
post-Sopranos on 12 episodes of Boardwalk
Empire, another gangland hit for HBO.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.980
Outside of acting, Chianese has a side career
as a tenor, which won't come as a surprise

00:03:57.989 --> 00:04:02.680
to Sopranos fans who watched him bring grown
mobsters to tears with his performance in

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.849
the Season 3 finale.

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:09.209
He hasn't giving up on acting—recent projects
include a remake of the postwar Italian masterpiece

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:10.200
Umberto D.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.700
James Gandolfini as Tony Soprano

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:17.660
The late James Gandolfini made his living
as a character actor before being cast in

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.860
the career-defining role of Tony Soprano.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.800
Following Gandolfini's 2013 death from a heart
attack while on vacation in Rome with his

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.530
family, Sopranos showrunner David Chase paid
tribute to his leading man, calling him a

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:30.040
"genius."

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.980
Gandolfini was on a real run when he passed,
appearing in five Rotten Tomatoes Certified

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.180
Fresh films in the space of two years…

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.980
"listen it sounds corny, but you broke my
heart.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.080
And I'm too old for that s---."

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.440
Thanks for watching!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.960
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

